{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361113-scenario-seeds-for-complex-relationships-white-elephant-for-chausse","id":1361113,"title":"Scenario Seeds for Complex Relationships (White Elephant for Chausse)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-15T11:22:59-08:00","id":1361113,"title":"Scenario Seeds for Complex Relationships (White Elephant for Chausse)","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350958-the-ninth-annual-exalted-white-elephant?p=1351053#post1351053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess I'll try it and be in !<br /> <br /> I love scenarios ideas for bound-together characters, usually with few players (2 or 3). Examples : The Dynast prodige and the Leftover, The Inseparable Solar and Lunar that can never reunite, etc ...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For Chausse, Here are a few seeds for bound together characters. Some are more generic, some are more specific. Hopefully at least one will pique your interest or give you some ideas to consider.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scenario 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sesus Faria, the new Dragon Blooded Satrap, has arrived to take control of the unruly satrapy of Mulberry. Her secretary, Violet River Blossom, is a mortal friend she\u2019s known since Primary school. Blossom is a native of the satrapy\u2026 and recently exalted as a Solar. She worries about being an Anathema and refuses to use her powers, but sometimes they leak out a bit. Ever since she Exalted, she\u2019s been having dreams of a girl she used to know in her village and feels driven to find her.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In Mulberry, the last Sesus Satrap had been squeezing them particularly hard and causing serious unrest, to the point that it caused Violet River Thistle to Exalt. This new Lunar escaped to the forest and has been helping local rebel groups, harrying silk shipments, and striking at Realm forces ever since. Unless Seuss Faria can calm things and bring peace to the region quickly, things will continue to escalate and, eventually Blossom will have to choose which side she wants to be on.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ultimately, someone is almost certainly going to have to fight an old friend.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scenario 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Two Dynasts have, as per their family\u2019s wishes, gotten married. But, unlike most other Realm marriages, this one wasn\u2019t to bring the two houses closer together, but instead so that they could spy on each other.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Why? Well perhaps they\u2019re both secretly agents of the All Seeing Eye and this is a test, before they\u2019re assigned to work together. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Or perhaps one is secretly an Iselsi and the other is a Sesus and the Sesus wants to know what House Iselsi is planning and the Iselsi needs to know how much House Sesus knows before they can murder their spouse.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scenario 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A sidereal has orders for these two people to have a strong relationship. As such they\u2019re now \u201ccoincidentally\u201d running into each other all the time and possibly feeling the first flutterings of attraction. And then the Sidereal steps up to the second part of her plan\u2026</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scenario 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A rash vow or a promise to your previous incarnation means you now have a Raksha who is acting like they\u2019re your significant other, be it romantically or platonically. Have fun with that.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scenario 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For as long as the village has existed, they have been protected by the Great Beast. In return, the Beast demands that the village provide it a villager as a sacrifice every generation. It is unknown what happens to this person. Most hope they become the servant to the Beast. All fear that they become the Beast\u2019s lunch.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The time has come again for the ...tribute, but\u2026. there has been no sign of the Beast for at least a moon. On the day of the tribute, two amongst those to be chosen erupted with power, one glowing gold and one glowing silver. Did they speak out against the Beast and have been cursed for their hubris...or rewarded for their bravery? How does the silver one react to their newfound memories of what the Beast has been doing to these villagers? What kind of relationship did these two have before and how is it complicated by them becoming Mates?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(alternately, maybe this year\u2019s sacrifice Exalts as the Solar Mate to the Great Beast. But that could be a bit of a squicky power/relationship dynamic, especially if the Great Beast HAS been eating the villagers.) </span><br /> <br /> </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T11:41:28-08:00","id":1361123,"title":"","content":"Thanks you for your time ! I'm off to read them immediately !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T11:58:10-08:00","id":1361127,"title":"","content":"I really really appreciate Sc\u00e9nario 5, this is exactly the kind of things I'm looking for in a Solar/lunar dual campaign, this seems fun.<br /> <br /> Scenario 4 is fun ! Could make an interesting solo, having a not-too-much-but-still-antagonistic Raksha could go a very long way here<br /> <br /> Scenario 2 reminds me of a movie that must be something like 10 years old (a blockbuster I think). I like the idea of having the 2 newlyweds spying on each other, I don't know why I really think I would play this kind of game as a comedy (like classical comedies of Moli\u00e8re and such, I don't know if non-french people know about them)<br /> <br /> I'm interested to see a play in Scenario 1 where the 3 major characters are all players characters, the campaign would be short but could be quite intense, and really put the social system to very good use !<br /> <br /> These scenarios are the exact reason I'm interested in seeing non-supernal Solars : some of them would blow up the whole scenario, while there is such a good potential here.<br /> <br /> I'm glad you found the time to write my White Elephant, thank you again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 01-15-2020, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T22:03:09-08:00","id":1361216,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sorry I wasn\u2019t quicker about it. I\u2019ve been planning on writing up scenario 1 more fully, so I 